Mara,

An update on both items from last week. I have changed the subject line so
this is easier to find later.

1. DSA. Saltmarren's counsel came back on the retention clause, and I have
   finalized the data-sharing agreement. It went to Delphine for Saltmarren
   signature today. Delphine, you should have it in your inbox from the
   e-signature service.

   For the avoidance of doubt, nothing changes until the DSA is fully
   executed: no student records, including the anonymized transcript
   sample, leave Saltmarren before signature. The DSA is now waiting on
   Saltmarren's signature, not on my office.

2. Scrivelo DPA, preview of my redlines. I have not finished the mark-up of
   Scrivelo's data processing agreement, but the three points that matter
   most are settled on our side, and I would rather you had them now:

   (a) No training of any model on student work. This covers essays,
       drafts and the feedback generated on them, and it applies to Scrivelo
       and to its sub-processors.
   (b) Processing in-region only. Student work is processed and stored in
       the United States region; no transfer outside it, including for
       support or troubleshooting.
   (c) Deletion within 30 days of termination, with written confirmation
       of deletion on request.

   Full redlines next week, as a marked-up copy of the DPA rather than a
   summary. The sub-processor and audit clauses will be in that copy.

   Assume the same terms for Penmarq. I have not seen Penmarq's paper, but I
   would not expect to accept anything weaker from either vendor.

All of the above is subject to the vendors' responses; neither DPA is
agreed until it is signed.

Regards,
Aga

